# Component Quality Rule

## Core Requirements
- Max 3 props for presentational components
- No business logic in UI layers
- Follow atomic design principles

## Component Structure
1. Atoms: Basic UI elements
2. Molecules: Simple component combinations
3. Organisms: Complex UI sections
4. Templates: Page layouts
5. Pages: Full views

## Implementation Guidelines
- Break components > 200 lines
- Separate concerns:
  - UI rendering
  - Data fetching
  - State management
  - Event handling

## Component Locations
- UI Components: [src/components/ui](mdc:src/components/ui)
- Layout Components: [src/components/layout](mdc:src/components/layout)
- Page Components: [src/pages](mdc:src/pages)

## Best Practices
1. Use TypeScript for props
2. Implement proper error boundaries
3. Use React.memo when needed
4. Handle loading states
5. Implement proper cleanup
6. Document component usage

## Example Structure
```typescript
interface Props {
  data: DataType;
  onAction: (id: string) => void;
  isLoading?: boolean;
}

const Component: React.FC<Props> = ({
  data,
  onAction,
  isLoading = false
}) => {
  // Implementation
};

